# Storm-the-Core finale. Multiple factions converge on the
# MotherboardCore location. The Motherboard performer holds court.

== storm_core
  cast: NineIron
  setting: NineIronHide

NINEIRON
  (improv duration: 30s, advance on: quorum(4) [gesture(stand)])
  (Stand. Say only: "Then come on.")

<broadcast: cohort(Defectors)>
  NARRATOR
    The defectors move. Anyone still in a faction camp can choose
    to follow. The Plaza door is open. The corridor is short. The
    hum gets louder.

* Defectors arrive at the Core.
  -> motherboard_intro

== motherboard_intro
  cast: Motherboard
  setting: MotherboardCore

<broadcast: location(MotherboardCore)>
  NARRATOR
    The Core is a room that is a computer. There is a chair. In the
    chair is a thing that looks like a person who has been editing
    themselves for a long time.

MOTHERBOARD
  (improv duration: 180s, advance on: quorum(6) [speech(go), gesture(Cue)])
  (Greet them by faction. Address each cohort separately. Make
   offers that match their cohort: Chatters get "a stage forever,"
   Mods get "the seat at the calibration desk," Defectors get "your
   own bodies back." Take questions. Lie about exactly one thing —
   audience must choose which.)

# Three endings, decided by who's in the room and who flinches.

* The Defectors charge — keys produced, chair shorted.
  -> ending_destroyed
* A Mod takes the calibration seat.
  -> ending_mod_succession
* A Chatter takes the offer of "a stage forever."
  -> ending_chatter_assimilated
* Everyone refuses everything and walks out.
  -> ending_walked_late
